/* Bible Explorer Kids — shared service worker for the whole bundle
   (index + scene1 + scene2 + scene3). Gives returning/!first-load kids
   instant loads and instant scene-to-scene jumps by runtime-caching
   same-origin assets, plus offline resilience.

   IMPORTANT: bump CACHE_VERSION whenever you change game assets/code so
   returning kids get the fresh files instead of a stale cache.

   Note: an earlier inline blob:-URL service worker in scene1 never actually
   registered (modern browsers reject blob: SW scripts), so this external
   file is the first working SW. It only runs over http(s)/localhost — on a
   file:// build it simply never registers (harmless). */
const CACHE_VERSION = 'bek-bundle-v97'; // v97: U batch (Jane 2026-06-22 phone playtest) — (1) FULLSCREEN: on the FIRST user gesture every scene now best-effort requests fullscreen (window._goFullscreen, attached to pointerdown/touchstart/keydown/click), reclaiming the mobile browser chrome ("white tab") so the game gets the whole screen — also gives LANDSCAPE more vertical room / line of sight. Page nav exits fullscreen so each scene re-requests on its first tap; graceful no-op where unsupported (iOS Safari). (2) SPOT-DIFF HALO COORDS corrected from a fresh A-vs-B PIXEL DIFF (_spotdiff.py): "moses running" was badly off — scene3 entries had (20,30)+(12,49) pointing at UNCHANGED pixels (missing 2 of the 4 real diffs); scene1/scene2 had a wrong (24,3x). All "moses running" now (17,41),(43,58),(84,57),(55,82). "moses in nile" 4th coord (47,67)/(51,70)→(54,68) in all entries. (This is the portrait "halos in incorrect positions" — they were data-wrong, not a render bug; the well + princess coords were already correct/fixed.) (3) COVER "Personal Best" panel: empty Collections/Progress SECTIONS were rendering as big blank framed cards (the "empty rectangle" on phones) — now a whole section is hidden when it has no earned chips; section labels bumped 11→13px + brighter gold and chips 14→15px for small-device readability. // v96: T batch (Jane 2026-06-22 playtest #2) — (1) SEQUENTIAL GATE hardened: a typed URL (e.g. scene3_midian.html?from=scene2) used to GRANT progress and let kids skip scenes. Now Scene 1/2 set bek.bundle1.progress on their real showWin, and the gates REQUIRE genuine progress (Scene2 needs >=1, Scene3 needs >=2); ?from= only skips the cover, never unlocks. Verified: scene3 with progress=0 (with or without ?from=scene2) bounces to scene1 and grants nothing; progress=2 loads. (2) SCENE-1 "Moses at the well" SPOT-DIFF clue corrected — coords were right (pixel-diffed) but the clue named the wrong things (rope/palm/dune/sand); now names the actual diffs: orange daughter in the middle, the bucket on the well, the bag at the foot of the well, the shepherd on the far right. (3) PRINCESS-RESCUE (baby Moses) spot-diff clue fixed in ALL scenes to: crown on the princess, dress colour of the servants, the dragonfly, swaddle colour of baby Moses (coords nudged to the pixel-diff centres). (4) AMBIGUOUS verse question (Scene 2, "moses with sheep"): option A "Exodus 2:15 — fled to Midian" also read true for a shepherding picture; swapped to "Exodus 2:11 — Moses saw an Egyptian beating a Hebrew" so only D (Exodus 3:1, tending the flock) fits, + clearer clue. (5) SECTION-4 narration slideshow now lingers ~1s after each clip ends before advancing, so it's a touch slower and stays in sync with the audio. (6) SCENE-2 OASIS-BY-THE-CAMEL reachable: the oasis heart tile is at (17,15) and the camel STARTED on it (tx17) patrolling cols 15-26, so its solid body blocked it; moved the patrol east (tx21, minTx19) so col 17 is always free. (7) JIGSAW PAUSE LOCK fixed: pausing during the 800ms before the "torn caravan map" opened let the jigsaw open OVER the pause modal (state='puzzle' so Resume did nothing) — the jigsaw now WAITS until un-paused; and restartScene now hard-stops the jigsaw bg music (puzzleBg) which used to keep looping after a restart. (8) RESCUE on HARD eased: shepherds arrive much less frantically (spawnEvery 0.90s→1.05s) + slower foes (72→66) + fewer waves (34→30); still the toughest tier. Confirmed the Scene-3 final win modal already fires confetti + a gold glitter burst. // v95: S batch (Jane 2026-06-22 playtest screenshots) — (1) CERTIFICATE overlap REALLY fixed: the canvas drew the name/rank/score values at x=0.26W, but the template's blank underlines (measured) START at x=0.336W, so the values sat ON TOP of the printed NAME/RANK/SCORE labels. Moved values to x=0.345W (just inside the line), maxW 0.40W (clears the line end 0.763W + the gold seal at 0.773W). Verified by canvas pixel-sampling: value text now lives in the 0.345–0.62W band with a CLEAN gap before the labels (zero dark px 0.322–0.345W). (2) BROWN "hand-drawn creatures" GONE for good: the sheep sprites are now BAKED to white wool at build time (_whiten_sheep.py recolors sheep/lamb PNGs avg 207,187,157→~233,230,225, originals backed up to assets/images/_orig_sheep) and the unreliable runtime ctx.filter (which silently no-ops on some mobile browsers, leaving them tan) was REMOVED from both _drawOneSheep + drawScene3RescueFlock. (3) RESCUE TREASURE BAGS now ADD TO THE HUD: openRescueGame captures bagsAtOpen; on a 7/7 win _closeRescue flies the WHOLE session's net bag gain (replays included) into the HUD wallet via _flyTreasureBagsToHud + counts up (verified 90→357), and every other exit path (partial/lose/quit) refreshes updateHudTreasure so the wallet is never stale. CONFIRMED the scene-3 win modal already aggregates the bags (showWin→_bankSceneBests reads game.treasureBags BEFORE _renderJourneyPanel). (4) JETHRO TENT INTERACTION: reaching the tent now shows a Jethro WELCOME modal (his portrait + "make your home with my family") that BLESSES Moses with +15 stars (one-time, banked at win). (5) SCENE-2 CARAVAN TRADER now ALWAYS gives +5 stars on first meeting (+1 heart too if hurt) with short crisp dialog — was "just a heal, no points" at full hearts vs not. (6) NARRATION delayed-start fixed: per-panel clips were `new Audio(url)` cold elements that DOWNLOADED before playing (the "late start / seemed to need a click"); now WARM-CACHED (preload='auto'+load, all 10 opening+section-4 clips warmed up front, next clip warmed on each panel) so a beat plays instantly. (7) MAIN-MENU REPLAY audio no longer "blocked": the cover's audio-unlock listened only for 'click', but on replay/touch the first gesture is often pointerdown/touchstart with a suppressed click — now unlocks on pointerdown/touchstart/keydown/click (capture, once). // v94: VO + sheep batch (Jane 2026-06-22) — Scene-2 now plays the FIRST-vulture + FIRST-fox guidance VO (vo-s2-vulture.mp3 / vo-s2-fox.mp3, once each) when those hazards appear (they existed but were never wired). Scene-3 1st-wolf RESCUE-FLOCK: a freed sheep now RUNS WEST to safety and leaves the scene promptly (was ambling slowly EAST toward where the wolves came, so it read as "the sheep is still in the scene and doesn't run away"); confirmed the 2nd (pen) wolf raid already plays its wolf VO + tip popup. STILL OPEN: section-4 VO start-sync timing polish (on-device). // v93: certificate REBUILT as a CANVAS (template art + name/rank/score/date/seal drawn at exact pixel positions) — fixes the value text OVERLAPPING the baked-in NAME/RANK/SCORE labels, and replaces Print (which clipped) with a clean PNG "Download Certificate" button (toDataURL); verified no overlap (name starts at 26% — clear of the labels), download not tainted, responsive on phone. Scene-3 win modal now also fires a centered GOLD GLITTER BURST (+ the existing 64-piece confetti shower) so the victory is unmistakable. // v92: R batch (Jane 2026-06-21 playtest) — CERTIFICATE print no longer clips NAME/RANK/SCORE/seal (smaller fonts fit the fallback font + 8mm page margin). After the ENDING (Watch the Ending → closing+epilogue) now goes to MAIN MENU (scene1 hub), not left on frozen Scene 3 (epilogue button relabeled "Main Menu →"). Win-modal "congratulations" VO now WAITS for the fanfare to ring out in ALL 3 scenes (sequenced on the fanfare's 'ended', safety fallback). REMOVED win sound.mp3 from Scene-2 victory (levelUp+confetti carry it). Scene-2 + Scene-1 "Your Journey So Far" now show the aggregate ⭐ Points (the certificate score) — parity with Scene 3. Scene-3 OPENING narration: added the "Continue the Journey" tap-gate (navigating Scene2→3 carries no gesture, so autoplay blocked the narration — now the tap unlocks audio then the cinematic plays). Well-game LOCKED feedback is now a can't-miss banner ("Rescue the daughters first!") + optional guidance VO hook (vo-s3-locked.mp3, silent until recorded). End-narration bgm 0.05→0.03. STILL OPEN: section-4 VO start-sync polish; 1st-wolf 2nd-sheep flee; scene-2 vulture/fox + 2nd-wolf-raid VO triggers (maps exist, need wiring). // v91: O-batch finish (Jane 2026-06-21) — O13: Scene-3 controls now MATCH Scenes 1&2 in every orientation (ported _relocatePowerupsForOrientation: power-ups TOP strip on desktop/portrait, into .controls on landscape; bottom bar = actions LEFT + d-pad RIGHT desktop/portrait, d-pad LEFT + power-ups + actions RIGHT landscape) — verified all 3 modes. O11: on EASY difficulty the Bible clue AUTO-REVEALS in the challenge modal (Medium/Hard keep it behind the tap) — all 3 scenes. O5/O12: moses-home spot-diff clue corrected to the real 4 diffs (window, rolled-up fabric, bread on the table, candelabra). O2: confirmed the closing-narration bg music bed is 0.05 (ducks under voice); the 0.5 egyptianCover is only the end-journey celebration (no narration). O4/O6/O7/O9 re-audited = already done. // v90: certificate "Back to Game" (dropped kid into Scene 3) → "🏠 Main Menu" (Scene-1 hub) + replay nudge. G1: Scene1→2 section-4 narration now plays HANDS-FREE — each recorded beat auto-advances the image slideshow when it ends (was stuck on panel 1 with "no voiceover" because the cinematic never auto-advanced); Skip + final Continue both → Scene 2. Scene-1 LOADING BAR: the opening cinematic ended by calling startScene1() directly (no preload gate) → tutorial VO over a blank/slow canvas; now gated behind the preload bar (_beginScene1WhenReady, mirrors Scene 2). Scene-1 3 TUTORIAL texts aligned word-for-word to the recorded vo-s1-move/hide/gates narration. PHONE AUDIT FIX: Scene-2 portrait HUD forced flex-wrap:nowrap + overflow-x:auto at ≤420px, pushing MAP + Pause ~118px OFF-SCREEN (content 499px vs 375 viewport) — now wraps to 2 rows (stats group display:contents) so every HUD control is reachable; Scenes 1 & 3 HUDs already wrap (fine). // v89: Q batch (Jane 2026-06-21) — FORCES a full refresh; the prior cache was serving a stale MIX (some files new, some v88) so fixes didn't show + difficulty/cert/name looked broken even though the code was already correct. Ships: P2/P7 aggregation+certificate ROOT FIX (_liveRunValue banks the SAME number the HUD shows + monotonic bundle totals + cert falls back to live points), P10 8↔9 loop (epilogue "Get Certificate" → certificate.html, no victory-modal re-show), N3 kid-name prompt in scenes 2&3 when empty, P1 scene-3 timer freezes during narration/tip modals, P3 market-stall + Jethro-tent collision (was gated to game.scene===2 but Midian runs scene 3 → décor was walk-through), P4 kid-first truth-card copy, P5/P6 honest rescue toast + quit re-prompts. // v88: P batch partial (Jane 2026-06-20) — P8 FIXED: certificate printed BLANK because the art was a CSS background-image (browsers omit backgrounds from print/PDF) → now a real <img> (verified loads 1344x768 + overlays). P9: ending-narration bed (egyptianCover, sections 8&9) 0.12→0.05. STILL OPEN (need focused fresh pass, high regression risk): P2/P7 aggregation — journey + certScore read bek.bundle1.totalPoints written by _bankSceneBests from game._runAccum, which DIVERGED from the HUD treasure wallet (the 414); per-scene bests bank 0 for scenes finished before the model + no migration → cert "0 points", journey shows only just-finished scene. P10 sections 8↔9 loop (Get-Certificate re-opens victory modal → Watch-the-Ending). P1 scene-3 timer runs during narration/cutscene modals. P3 Moses walks onto market-stall tiles (collision). P4 truth-card copy not uplifting. P5 rescue says "all 7 rescued" when <7 saved. P6 mini-games' Quit-to-Midian leaves goal undone, exit not gated. N3 kid name empty on cert/victory. // v87: O batch start (Jane 2026-06-20) — O10 ROOT FIX for difficulty preservation: Scene 1's _beginAdventure now persists the actually-selected difficulty on Begin (the pill-click handler alone wasn't reliable), and the M4 'easy' band-aid default in scenes 2/3 was reverted to neutral 'medium'. Verified: Medium → bek.lastDifficulty='medium' → Scene 2 timeLimit 180 (3min). O1: modal-stacking guard (no popup over popup) now on ALL 3 scenes. REMAINING O items for next pass: O2 (lower bg on last 2 closing panels), O3 (Get-Certificate re-shows victory modal → section 8/9 loop), O4 (main-menu Truth Library + Power-Up Unlocks show only Scene-1 totals, not aggregate), O5 (moses-home spot-diff halo on bowls should be candelabra; 1st clue=window, last=candelabra), O6 (scene-2 close-call +2 pts like scene 1), O7 (purple victory VO after sfx — scene1/scene3), O8 (explain 82-treasures = sum of bests), O9 (scene-2 opening narration must fire at panel 1 + remove next btn + per-panel text sync), O11 (easier clues for hard questions), O12 (ALL spot-diff clues must list the actual differences), O13 (scene-3 dpad/buttons layout inconsistent with scenes 1/2), O14 (scene-3 market checkpoint 3rd Q = match-3 N7). // v86: N playtest batch (Jane 2026-06-20) — N1: Scene-2 mini-maze REALLY fixed (the board's 94% resolved against an auto-width flex wrapper so it never capped; now the WRAPPER is constrained to min(520px,92vw) and the board fills it with square cells — verified fits 480px modal at 63px cells). N4: removed "PANEL X of Y" from all narration captions. N5: Scene-3 opening narration force-loads + retries on interaction (was silent). N6: Scene-3 checkpoint modal shows a "?" (matches the on-map gold medallion) instead of checkpoint-1.png (Scene 2's red maze-glyph). N10: bgm-exit hard-stopped when the journey tracker opens (was bleeding in after Scene 3). N2: Scene-2 win narration now fires on the fanfare's 'ended' event (4.5s fallback) so it's never buried. STILL OPEN: N3 (player name — code reads bek.kidName correctly, empty when Scene-1 name prompt wasn't completed), N7 (match-3 ends too fast / Pharaoh-blaster win condition), N8 (well dialogue cut by rescue mini-game), N9 (You-did-it narration vs sfx — need the exact line). // v85: M playtest batch (Jane 2026-06-20) — M1: Scene-1 bgm-exit fixed for real (there were TWO _maybeSwapZoneMusic functions; the live one mapped the whole bottom stretch to bgm-exit → changed ZONE_BGM_KEY.exit to 'bgm', so bgm-exit only plays as the victory pad). M2: showTipPopup no longer stacks a popup over an open one (waits + retries). M3: Scene-2 opening narration force-loads + retries on first interaction. M4: scenes 2/3 difficulty fallback 'medium'(180)→'easy'(240) so Easy carries 4 min everywhere. M5: Scene-2 "Moses running" spot-diff vulture coord corrected to (17,41) + descriptive clue. M6: off-screen pursuit scouts (they chase from behind) now show a red "!" edge warning so they're never invisible. M7: TASKMASTERS unscramble clue made kid-easy (TASK+MASTERS). M8: Scene-2 mini-maze made responsive (caps to modal width, square cells) so it never clips. // v84: L playtest batch (Jane 2026-06-20) — Scene 3: removed phantom caves/"C" minimap pins; Quest modal shows Jethro's tent + checkpoint modals show the "?" tablet (image-icon support added to showTutorial/showTipPopup); "Desert"→"Bible/Midian" wording; "You did it" now celebrates with bgm-exit+sfx; removed win-sound + "missed N treasures"; certificate SCORE = total points; ending-narration music 0.25→0.12; removed the "X of 10 treasure bags" pickup toast; pair-question clues; dusk wolf flees on approach. CROSS-SCENE TREASURE MODEL reworked to SUM-OF-BEST-RUNS (per-scene bests in bek.scene{N}.{res}; bundle totals = sum of bests; replays reset + never double-count) in all 3 scenes. // v83: J+K playtest batches (Jane 2026-06-19) — bump FORCES every client to re-fetch assets/images + all 3 scene HTMLs, which is the real fix for K1/K6 ("oasis & exit images not loading"): the images load fine in a fresh build but the cache-first SW was serving a stale/incomplete v82 asset cache. This batch also ships: spot-the-difference real coords; Scene-2 power-up self-heal (reconcile on tick); lure now pulls BOTH guards and scouts to the decoy; chariot VO duck; bgm-exit only on the exit tile; Scene-2 win-modal audio cleanup; Scene-2 opening-narration tap-gate (autoplay gesture); mini-maze 72px; de-bleached prelude images; treasure-bag icon; clue verse-fallback; pause-aware scout grace; visible lure objects (goblet/rock/water-pot); checkpoint vector fallback. // v82: Unification batch (Jane 2026-06-14) — (1) ENTRY-POINT TRAP fixed: index.html was the OLD standalone all-in-one game (zero links to scene1) and manifest start_url '.'/folder-root resolved to it, so a QR/PWA launch loaded the dead legacy game; index.html now redirects to scene1_palace.html (old build saved as _legacy_allinone_backup.html) + manifest start_url->scene1_palace.html. (2) Scene-1 EXIT-CORRIDOR MUSIC was SILENT (audBgmExit pointed at a missing 'palace exit corridor.mp3'); repointed to bgm-exit.mp3. (3) ONE-WORLD DIFFICULTY 240/180/180 across all scenes (Scene-1 Hard 240->180; Scene-2 Medium 210->180, Hard 240->180; cover text/aria reconciled). (4) Scene-1 world-map sprites fixed (moses.png->'moses front facing.png', newmidian.png->'new midian.png'). (5) lesson-modal '*** ... ***' asterisks removed. (6) app name unified to "Moses' Deadly Escape" on Scene-1/Scene-2 tab title + meta + manifest. // v81: Scene-3 play-test batch (Jane 2026-06-09) — I drove the game in the harness and traced every item. THE WELL-CONFRONTATION CUTSCENE was the hub of several complaints: the recorded shepherd/Moses clips are genuinely long (4.8–8.6s each → ~30s total of FROZEN Moses), the sunset timer kept ticking the whole time (state stays 'playing'; only movement is frozen), and afterward the kid had to find + step onto the rescue billboard — which read as "can't launch the mini-game." FIXES: (1) the cutscene is now SKIPPABLE — tap/press (after a 0.9s grace) shows a pulsing "Tap to skip ▸" and ends it; (2) the SUNSET TIMER is FROZEN while the cutscene plays (no penalty for the forced dialogue — answers Jane's "should we freeze the timer?"); (3) on end (natural OR skip) the game flows STRAIGHT into the Rescue mini-game via openChallenge — no more billboard-hunting, which is the real fix for "still not able to launch the mini games while stepping on the billboard." Verified live: enter plaza → cutscene → timer frozen at 240 → skip → rescue modal opens. (4) CRYSTAL-MODAL NARRATION: the "those rude shepherds…go around them" line (and any onboarding line) now WAITS for a blocking modal (crystal reward / checkpoint / mini-game / win / danger / tip) to close before it speaks, so the voice always matches the screen. (5) WOLF-ATTACK BED no longer starts UNDER a crystal modal (same blocking-modal gate); it now hard-STOPS the instant the last wolf is shooed (1st raid) and the instant the pen is safe (2nd raid) instead of relying only on the per-frame sync. (6) 1st-raid ALL-CLEAR: a big can't-miss banner now tells kids the danger is over AND to "walk up close to your sheep to gather them, then lead the flock across" — they were crossing alone and the sheep wouldn't follow. (7) NARRATION HALF-CUT (from v80) confirmed via clip-length probe (clips are 4.8–8.6s; beats now hold the real length). The 2nd-wolf shoo modal + 2nd-raid music depend on the pen raid actually firing, which the v80 launch fix unblocks. // v80: Scene-3 batch (Jane 2026-06-09) — CRITICAL MINI-GAME LAUNCH + SLOWNESS: Jane diagnosed it perfectly (rescuetest=1 runs at correct speed, but launching from the billboard was SLOW / sometimes didn't launch). ROOT CAUSE: the _stateWatchdog (runs every loop, resets state 'dialog'->'playing' if no recognized modal is up) did NOT know about the rescueModal / wellPulleyModal, so it reset the state mid-launch — which (a) could break the launch and (b) resumed the HEAVY main maze loop so it competed with the mini-game's own rAF (two render loops = super slow; rescuetest=1 was fine because the maze world wasn't competing the same way). FIX: (1) the watchdog now recognizes rescueModal + wellPulleyModal as active modals (leaves the mini-game alone); (2) the main loop SKIPS render() entirely while a mini-game modal is active so the mini-game gets the full frame budget; (3) fixed a latent typo (document.getElement -> getElementById) that could throw inside the watchdog. This ALSO unblocks the 2ND WOLF (pen) RAID, which is gated on BOTH mini-games being solved — they couldn't be solved if they wouldn't launch. Verified live: watchdog preserves 'dialog' while the rescue modal is up, render-skip engages, rescue round runs at normal speed with no console errors. ALSO: (4) BG MUSIC vs CRYSTAL MODAL — the music started UNDER the crystal-reward modal because _closeChallengeModalAudio ran BEFORE the crystal modal was shown (so its crOpen guard missed it); the market/crystal close path now DEFERS the bgm resume to _resumeAfterClear (fires on the Continue tap) so music only starts after the crystal modal closes. (5) 2ND WOLF ATTACK now PROMPTS with the same modal + narration as the first wave (showTipPopup 'penraid' + the wolf voice line, repeat) instead of a bare toast. (6) NARRATION HALF-CUT — the well-confrontation cutscene beats had FIXED durations shorter than the recorded VO clips, so the next beat's playVoiceLine() cut the current shepherd/Moses line mid-word; each beat now holds at least its real clip length (+350ms) so the whole line is heard. (7) SHEPHERDS-COMING-NEAR alert: the two scout/shepherd PROXIMITY stings still played danger alert.mp3 — switched to _shepherdAlertSting() (alert.mp3) per Jane. // v79: Scene-3 batch (Jane 2026-06-08) — SHOO BAR (2nd raid): the red ring is on the WOLF but the tap only hit-tested SHEEP — now hit-tests the ringed pen wolf directly + wider sheep radius. BGM VOLUME REGRESSION: the shepherd sting was ducking the bgm and nesting with the voice-duck, leaving the music stuck quiet — the shepherd sting NO LONGER touches the bgm (only dialogue/narration duck it); alert.mp3 plays one-shot (no loop), quiet, over normal bgm, cut the instant Moses walks away. BROWN SHEEP: brightened + desaturated the sheep sprite render so the cream/tan PNGs read WHITE (not "brown hand-drawn animals"). TENT EXIT (recurring): added a per-frame proximity check — standing in the tent DOOR ZONE (door tile + west approach) with all gates solved completes the scene, so no more buried/grid-locked tile-hunting; sealed state shows a clear banner naming what's left. Removed overhead toasts: "Checkpoint activated!", "you crossed the stream…", "a clay jar shatters", and the misleading oasis "+1 heart restored" messages. Moved the WOOLY-WAY pen board (14,13)→(20,18) and the travel bread (15,13)→(4,16) OFF the crossing path. Well-lock "error" while parked on the Water-the-Flock tile is now throttled (5s) + a gentle pop. MINI-GAME SPEED: rescue foes faster (foeSpeed 40-52→56-72) + quicker spawns; pulley match-point slow-mo shortened 1.4→0.55. (Tutorial confirmed first-time-only + goal audio on replay.) // v78: Scene-3 QUEUE batch (Jane 2026-06-07) — (1) MINI-GAME SLOW-MO: the well game's match-point slow-mo (_pulley.slowmo=1.4) was never cleared on win/lose, so a replay ran at 50% speed — now reset in _pulleyWin/_pulleyLose. (2) COUNTDOWN desync: the visual 3-2-1 lasted a fixed 3.0s while the audio is shorter ("music ended, then 3-2-1 showed") — the visual countdown now lasts EXACTLY the raceCountdown.mp3 duration in BOTH games, so they run + finish together. (3) TRUTH CARD now feeds the cross-scene SCROLL total (+1) so the "scroll count 0" actually moves (Scene-1 parity). (4) FEWER PALMS around the well (~1/6 cover tiles, favor pastoral olive/terebinth) + crisp high-smoothing render; the palm is solid COVER, not a heart-restore (that's the tile-6 oasis). (5) REMOVED the east-bank boulders + rockpile so the path after the river crossing is clear. (6) ENDING narration panels BRIGHTENED (brightness 1.14 + saturate/contrast — were "very dull"). (7) WIN MODAL split: "📜 Print Certificate" opens the certificate DIRECTLY (no forced narration); new "🎬 Watch the Ending" plays the closing+epilogue narration then returns to the win modal; the closing no longer auto-plays before the certificate. (8) HINT/CLUE now a GOLD glittery banner + sparkles + chime (was a plain toast). (9) sheep-pen SIGN enlarged 1.7→2.3 tiles. // v77: shoo-bar, hint, shepherd alert, wolf modal, dedup, chest, heart SFX — (1) SHOO BAR on 2nd (pen) raid: _wolfShoo.open got stuck true after the first raid, so the tap early-returned and no shoo bar showed; added a SELF-HEAL (if the flag's true but the overlay isn't actually visible, clear it) in both the tap handler + the modal-open gate. (2) HINT was wrong: it jumped to "reach the tent" the moment the flock crossed (scene3Herd.done) even with mini-games unfinished — now mini-game-aware (points to rescue/water with the WHY) and the TENT "sealed" message now names exactly what's left (rescue/water) as a banner. (3) SHEPHERD ALERT audio: was too loud + played the whole long alert.mp3 over the bgm — now quieter (vol 0.30), ducks the bgm while it sounds, auto-cuts after 1.6s, and stops the instant Moses leaves the shepherd's radius. (4) WOLF/"Watch the Flock" modal no longer fires before a wolf is actually attacking — gated to a live first-wave raid + a real wolf. (5) REPEATING QUESTIONS: ported Scene 1's within-run de-dup (exclude already-used question IDs) into Scene 3's bundle padding. (6) TRUTH CHEST moved off (32,12) — it sat UNDER Jethro's tent — to (28,12) on the open approach so it's visible. (7) clear HEART-LOSS cue (uh-oh sting + heart-HUD red pulse) on the charging ram + campfire so a lost heart is obvious. // v76: BROWN CREATURES SOLVED — using the ?dbg=1 labeller + canvas pixel-sampling, the mystery "brown creatures" are the STRANDED HERD SHEEP (white sheepLeft/lamb PNGs that render warm cream/tan ~225,199,157 in daylight and dim to dark brown ~128,83,49 on the pause screen). ROOT ISSUE: their graze-wander had NO row bound, so they drifted UP into the marketplace and read as random brown animals before the kid had any context. Constrained the wander to rows 9-17 (their river-bank spawn band) so the flock stays DOWN BY THE RIVER where it belongs. Verified: herd spawns + stays rows 9-14. // v75: debug sprite labeller (?dbg=1) // v74: Scene-3 batch (Jane 2026-06-07) — DEBUG sprite labeller added behind ?dbg=1 (zero footprint otherwise) to identify the mystery "brown creatures": it prints each drawn animal/NPC sprite's IMG key on the canvas. In testing every animal renders correctly (herd sheep = white sheepLeft/sheepRight/lamb/lambAlt PNGs, goat black-white, wolf grey, fox disabled) and all procedural fallbacks (wolf/sheep/fox) are removed, so the brown creatures couldn't be reproduced — the labeller lets Jane screenshot them with ?dbg=1 so we can name them. // v74: Scene-3 batch (Jane 2026-06-07) — (1) "Welcome to Midian, Moses!" restored to the Your-Quest tutorial text (matches vo-s3-goal). (2) HUD "2/5 after rescuing all sheep": updateHudFlock's herd condition was gated on !scene3Herd.done, so when the last sheep penned the chip flipped back to the pasture tally — removed the gate, now reads 5/5. (3) "Going into the tent doesn't work / have to maneuver": the win fired only on the single topmost exit tile, but the tent door spans 2 exit tiles — now ANY east-edge exit tile (nx>=MAP_W-3) ends the scene (river stepping-stones excluded). (4) WOLF-RAID AUDIO: the bgm-corridor + alert loop "kept playing all over" because it's only stopped from updateScene3Herd (runs only while playing) — added _killWolfRaidBed() on mini-game open + win so it can't bleed into another screen; looping alerts (wolfAlert/alerted/wolfEpic/challengeMusic/bgmExit) now ALSO duck under a voice line; the shepherd sting won't fire while a raid bed or narration is already sounding (one alert at a time). (5) egyptian-cover-music volume halved 0.5->0.25 so the closing narration is audible. (6) onboarding TIP/tutorial modal text now matches the recorded voiceover (shepherd/river/flock + 3 steps). (7) removed the procedural brown desert-fox silhouette fallback (only the real PNG renders). // v73: Scene-3 narration fixes (Jane 2026-06-07) — (1) "i didn't hear any voiceover": the bg music + sfx were OVERPOWERING the lines AND a scoping bug meant the ducking never ran (playVoiceLine called _beginVoiceDuck with `a` declared inside a different try-block → ReferenceError swallowed). Fixed the scope + added AUDIO DUCKING: while a voice line plays, every music loop ducks to 0.05 and SFX are suppressed (voice + UI clicks still pass), restored on the clip's 'ended'. (2) "modal text doesn't match the voiceover": the onboarding TIP popups (shepherd/river/flock) + the 3-step TUTORIAL now play the MATCHING recorded line AND their on-screen text is rewritten to say the same words (e.g. shepherd modal now reads "...they can't hurt Moses. Just go around them." = vo-s3-shepherd). Tutorial steps speak move/goal/checkpoint; goal voiceover no longer double-fires (tutorial owns it; returning kids get it post-pan). Verified live: ducking engages (bgm 0.6→0.05, sfx blocked), modal body == voiceover text, no console errors. // v72: Scene-3 UX pass — VOICE-FIRST ONBOARDING (Jane 2026-06-06): wired Jane's 16 vo-s3-*.mp3 recordings to play JUST-IN-TIME, ONCE each, single-channel (no overlap) — goal (scene start), checkpoint (first market gate), shepherd (first taunt), wolf (first grab), river (first reach), crossing (built), rescue + well (entering each mini-game), tent (both minis done), and per-power-up on first use (jar/speed/freeze; truthSeeker/scribesWisdom fall back to the generic line until recorded). ONE-LINE GOAL BANNER on each phase change (reuses _showCrossingBanner). SMART HINT button now shows the current phase objective + a LIVE direction to the next target (nearest market checkpoint → cross river → rescue → water → tent) instead of a generic line. vo-s3-win NOT wired (the existing "congratulations scene 3" plays — avoids overlap per Jane). Verified live: lines play once each via playVoiceLine, objective + hint correct, no console errors. // v71: Scene-3 SHOW-STOPPER (Jane 2026-06-06) — entering the WELL/RESCUE standalone billboards loaded the WRONG checkpoint mini-game on top. Root cause: the gate STEP-ON trigger in attemptMove runs an "aggressive _forceShow" that force-activates the QUESTION challengeModal if it isn't visible 30/100/250 ms after opening a gate — a Scene-1 fix for "challenge not triggering." But well/rescue gates launch their OWN standalone modals (wellPulleyModal/rescueModal) via openChallenge and never use challengeModal, so _forceShow force-showed the gate's vestigial 3rd-question mini-game (maze/memory/etc.) over the standalone game (and the 500ms bailout even marked the gate solved+skipped). Now the force-show + bailout run ONLY for question-checkpoint (market) gates. Verified live: stepping onto the rescue gate opens the rescue game (challengeModal NOT force-shown); stepping onto the well gate opens the well game — both PASS. // v70: Scene-3 batch (Jane 2026-06-06) — SHOW-STOPPER mini-game soft-lock FIXED: the match-3 checkpoint game put its "advance + safety timer" INSIDE the _sugarCrushAll() finale callback, so if that finale never fired (throttled timers/throw) the checkpoint never advanced and the kid was stuck on the cleared board with only EXIT. Hoisted a GUARANTEED top-level 4.2s advance (sort + collector games were already safe; crystal-reward Continue verified working). START-IMAGE DRIFT during the intro camera pan fixed: _safeAnchorX reads window._introPanActive but Scene 3 only set the LOCAL var, so the start art slid with the camera — now sets the window flag too (matches Scene 2's fix). TIMER consistency: Hard difficulty 120s→180s (Easy 240 / Med 180 / Hard 180 per Jane). WHITE HAND-DRAWN SHEEP removed: drawScene3RescueFlock no longer draws the cream fillRect fallback (real sheep PNG only). CIRCLED BROWN BOX removed: the marketplace 'tent' décor at (2,2) had no PNG and fell back to a crude procedural brown trapezoid (drawDesertTent) clashing with the 3D art — décor entry removed. Well-cut "A commotion at the well!" overhead toast removed (it overlapped the cutscene speech bubbles/banner). // v69: Scene-3 finish batch (Jane 2026-06-06) — GRID-LOCK: a kid could get boxed in with no legal move (clustered market-stall décor + an NPC sealing the tile). Added an anti-soft-lock escape valve in attemptMove: when EVERY neighbour is blocked, Moses squeezes out past décor/an NPC, but never through a real wall, the river, or the tent (verified: boxed→escapes, not-boxed→décor still blocks). #6 SHOO on the 2nd (pen) raid: removed the over-tight TILE*2.2 proximity gate in the tap hit-test so tapping ANY penned/following sheep opens the shoo modal (the pen raid already guarantees a live wolf; modal targets the nearest). #7 2nd attack back-to-back: the well+rescue mini-game gate now FAILS CLOSED (was skipped when challengeGates was empty, arming the raid right after the crossing). #8 HUD sheep chip froze on the pasture tally during the river crossing — now shows the live crossing count (scene3Herd.across/total), switched on when the crossing builds + updated as each sheep reaches the pen (verified: chip reads 0/5 at crossing start). #11 OASIS: the maze horizon used scene3_background.png — a DESERT OASIS (dunes + palms + a well) clashing with the green pasture; replaced with a procedural GREEN rolling-hills horizon (verified: no desert/palms/well, world reads as one green meadow). #5 pasture-flock wolf-leave confirmed working live; herd/pen wolf flee→gone is structurally correct (timed crossing needs on-device confirm — headless preview throttles the game's per-frame loop). // v68: Scene-3 #9 TENT COLLISION (Jane 2026-06-06) — Moses could walk through the UPPER THIRD of Jethro's tent: the tent sprite is ~4 tiles tall (peak + body, rows door-1..door-4) but the solid footprint was only 2 tall (rows door-1..door-2), leaving the shoulders/peak (rows door-3..door-4) walkable. Extended _getTentBodyTiles to the full 4-tall body; verified live (cols 31-33 rows 8-11 now all solid, door + front approach still walkable, exit still reachable). Also: game NAME standardized to "Moses' Deadly Escape" (tab title, cover, meta) — was "Moses' Escape to Midian", mismatching the Etsy listing + certificate. // v67: Scene-3 gameplay batch (Jane 2026-06-06) — #3 shepherd-approach sting now plays alert.mp3 (bossAlert), not danger alert.mp3. #4 CLUE MISROUTING fixed: added explicit kid-friendly clue: fields to the 9 Scene-3 questions that had none (s3e1/3/4/5/7/8/10/11/12), so the hint engine stops keyword-falling-back to the wrong "Midian (Ex 2:15)" clue — verified live (the "how many daughters" question now shows the seven-daughters Ex 2:16 clue). #2 BGM-vs-victory clash: all 6 direct audio.bgm.play() resume paths (wolf-raid end, well/rescue close/quit) now route through setMusic('bgm') so bgm DEFERS until the success/levelUp fanfare ends instead of clashing. #10 BROWN HAND-DRAWN WOLVES: _drawFlockWolf no longer draws the procedural dark blob when wolf*.png isn't loaded yet (covers all 3 wolf systems — pasture flock, river raid, pen raid); only the real grey-wolf PNG renders, with a soft contact shadow on the rare pre-load frame. // v66: ASSET-WEIGHT pass (Jane 2026-06-06) — every image in assets/images recompressed for phones: backgrounds/panels 256-color palette-quantized, transparent sprites RGB-quantized with ORIGINAL 8-bit alpha preserved (soft edges intact), tiles/sprites capped to display size. assets/images 210MB->70MB (total 252MB->116MB); the midian grass tile alone 2.6MB->60KB, so the floor/backdrop/sprites land near-instantly on cellular instead of flashing/blank. Filenames unchanged (zero reference edits). ADDED install-time PRECACHE of the Scene-3 opening shell (HTML + grass/backdrop/moses/wolf/sheep/intro/tent) via allSettled so the first screen is instant + offline-safe on returning devices; rest still cache-first on demand. // v65: Scene-3 fix-all pass (Jane 2026-06-06) — SLOW LOAD: the Midian floor fell back to the desert SAND tile while "midian grass tile.png" loaded, flashing yellow desert ~10s; now the green meadow base shows immediately (sand fallback skipped in Midian), grass layers on when ready. OASIS around the well fully cleared: removed the remaining pasture palms + the reed clusters ringing the well pool/village (MAP tile-3 → open grass). 2ND WOLF ATTACK now only fires AFTER both well+rescue mini-games are cleared (was slamming in right after "all sheep safe"). Shooed pasture wolf now RUNS OFF the scene instead of freezing. uh-oh.mp3 plays every time Moses bumps the river before earning 3 crystals (throttled). A short alert sting plays when a shepherd gets close (one-shot, never looping over the bgm). // v64: Scene-3 hotfix (Jane 2026-06-06) — (1) BGM-vs-victory clash REALLY fixed: the challenge-close audio resumed bgm with a direct audio.bgm.play() that bypassed the setMusic victory-defer; now the challenge-close skips bgm while the crystal-reward modal is open, and the crystal modal's Continue (_resumeAfterClear) resumes bgm via setMusic('bgm') which waits for the success-trumpet/level-up fanfare to finish. (2) MINI-GAME SOFT-LOCK guard: the sort/match-3/collector games finished via _gameCrystalClimax(onDone); if that callback ever failed the checkpoint never advanced and the kid was stuck on "All sorted!" with only Exit — added a one-shot advance + 2.8s safety timer to all three so a mini-game can never trap the player. // v63: Scene-3 queue cleanup (Jane 2026-06-06) — SHEPHERDS: red proximity halo removed (they never cost a heart); Moses can no longer stand ON a shepherd (attemptMove blocks it); shepherds STOP bothering + slink away once both well+rescue mini-games are solved. FLOCK "3 saved / 3 lost" miscount fixed (each sheep now resolves once — guard against double-free from run-at-wolf + tap-SHOO both firing). AUDIO: wolf attack now freezes the bgm and plays bgm-corridor.mp3 as a single danger bed (no track collision); bgm-exit.mp3 heat-up sting under the scene-complete banner; win modal plays win-confetti-sparkle.mp3 + a DOM confetti shower; post-Scene-3 closing+epilogue narration uses the lively egyptian-cover-music.mp3 bed; added the audConfetti/audBgmExit/audBgmCorridor/audEgyptianCover elements. "Why did the daughters come to the well?" got a real kid clue. // v62: Scene-3 anger-batch fixes (Jane 2026-06-06) — HAND-DRAWN BROWN SHEEP removed: deleted the procedural fallback in BOTH sheep drawers (_drawOneSheep + decorative drawScene3Flock) so only the real sheep.png ever renders (the brown blob was the "moving brown hand-drawn sheep" Jane saw crossing; jars were NOT it — restored later). MAP "(2)" badge removed — ported Scene 1's plain "MAP" button (peek was already unlimited). BGM-vs-victory collision fixed centrally in setMusic(): when a checkpoint's 3rd-question fanfare (successTrumpet/levelUp) is still sounding, the bgm loop now DEFERS until it ends. Removed the "A distant wolf howls in the dusk..." overhead toast (kept the howl sound). Disabled the shepherd flock-scatter raid that made the flock un-crossable. Cinematic panel-info ("PANEL x of y" + counters) removed; "His sons grew tall" -> "His son grew tall". // v61: REAL printable certificate (Jane 2026-06-06) — built certificate.html on top of Jane's "certificate template.png" art: overlays the kid's NAME (from bek.kidName, captured in Scene 1) + RANK (star tier) + SCORE (stars/points) + date onto the template's blank lines, adds a gold Bible-Explorer-Kids seal, and is print / Save-as-PDF ready (landscape @page, toolbar hidden on print). showWin() now stores bek.certRank + bek.certScore; the win-modal certificate button opens certificate.html instead of the wrong GAME_ACCESS_CARD.html. // v60: Scene-3 live-test batch 3 partial (Jane 2026-06-06) — #5 SHEEP CAN'T CROSS fixed: removed the west-post shepherd flock-scatter raid that reset following sheep back to grazing faster than the kid could lead them ("a shepherd scattered a sheep!"), so the flock-across counter stuck at 0/5 — the wolf raid still supplies the thrill; the flock now crosses smoothly. #13 removed the panel-info captions ("PANEL X of Y") + numeric "X of Y" counters from all three narration cinematics (opening/closing/epilogue); kept the scripture eyebrow on panel 1. #21 epilogue typo "His sons grew tall" -> "His son grew tall" (matches the audio). (More of batch 3 in progress: audio sequencing/music beds, win-modal confetti+totals, challenge selection highlight, MAP "(2)" badge, Interact SFX, shepherds-stop-after-minigames, treasure-chest image, hand-drawn ram, certificate.) // v59: Scene-3 live-test batch 2 (Jane 2026-06-06) — #163 DÉCOR COLLISION: market stalls / boulders / fruit trees / tent / cookfire / rock cairns are now SOLID (isWalkable consults a cached décor-tile set) so Moses routes AROUND every object instead of walking through it; verified START->EXIT + every pickup still reachable once the crossing is built (no softlock). #170 the post-candy-crush "A stepping-stone to cross the river!" sub-line was cream-on-bright and washed out — given the same crisp white + heavy dark-brown outline as the .gcx-label above it. #164 victory + scene-complete + 2-star headline said "reached the WELL"; all now say "reached Jethro's tent". #165 the herd crosses + reaches the pen faster (distance-aware catch-up for stragglers + tighter conga gap 7->4). #166 thinned the NE pasture palm "oasis" cluster around the well (4 cover-palms -> open grass). #167 narration/cinematic panels (opening, closing, epilogue) now turn with the Scene-1 page-turn SFX (added audPageTurn + audio.pageTurn). #168 the tiny/blurry flock signpost ("sheep board") enlarged ~1.0->1.7 tiles + crisp high-smoothing render. #169 softened the sheep-pen floor to a subtle worn tint (was a jarring earth patch) — the bold rope fence carries the readability. #172 removed the two marketplace terracotta jar piles ("brown creatures" Jane circled by the stalls). // v58: Scene-3 regression batch (Jane 2026-06-05) — #162 match-3 "pharaoh crystal clears the WHOLE board on one swap" fixed: expandClears() is now SEED-ONLY (a cross fires exactly its row+column, a colour bomb clears one kind, and any blaster merely caught in a blast is cleared as an ordinary tile instead of recursively chain-detonating across the entire 6×6 board — bounded, Candy-Crush style). #161 sheep pen invisible after crossing — the pen is now drawn with a warm packed-earth floor + a BOLD rope enclosure (west gate gap + corner/gate posts) ALWAYS, with the stone-wall PNG layered on top, so it reads as a pen even when the wall sprite is cache-stale. #160 same-tile overlap (a shepherd / "scout" standing on the vendor) — every shepherd movement branch (patrol, chase, jar-decoy lure) now refuses to step onto a standing NPC's tile. #159 post-crossing congestion — the 7 decorative grazing sheep that used to scatter across the crossing→pen→well corridor are cut to a 3-sheep cluster beside Jethro's tent, so only the real herd sheep are in the action. #157 hard-bank checkpoint clues all carry explicit kid-friendly clues now (clue fix complete across easy/medium/hard). #152 rescue-game background no longer falls back to the well's desert image. THIS BUMP ALSO REFRESHES the stale-v57 asset cache that made shepherds / sheep / wolves / trees render as procedural fallbacks on returning devices (#153 / #154 / #155 / #156). // v57: Scene-3 treasure-bag ECONOMY (item 16) — removed the phantom default-80 rescue purse (rescue now opens at the kid's ACTUAL accumulated bags = game.treasureBags bank), reduced the per-checkpoint grant to a modest seed (easy 30 / medium 25 / hard 20 — "not a lot but enough to get started"), repurposed the HUD treasure chip as a WALLET that shows the live bank (hid the misleading /10 pickup denominator), and added a bag-FLIGHT + count-up animation (_flyTreasureBagsToHud) so the bags earned on a 3rd-question solve visibly fly into and increment the HUD counter; plus scene1/scene2 undeployed polish. // v56: RETINA/DPR maze-render fix (all 3 scenes) + Scene-3 bundle-flow polish — (a) the per-frame transform reset in render()/_renderInner() was hard-resetting to identity (setTransform(1,0,0,1,0,0)), discarding the device-pixel-ratio scale that resizeCanvas() set, so on retina PHONES (dpr 2-3) the whole maze world rendered at 1x into the TOP-LEFT QUADRANT of the 2x backing store — exposing the painted backdrop and reading to Jane as "Scene 3 is showing a background image instead of the midian grass tile." Fixed by remembering dpr in a module var (_renderDPR) and re-applying ctx.setTransform(_renderDPR,...) each frame; desktop dpr=1 is a no-op (no regression). Maze now fills the canvas edge-to-edge with the tiled midian grass floor on portrait/landscape/desktop. (b) Scene 3 was the only scene WITHOUT an auto-launch block, so the bundle flow (Scene 2 journey tracker -> scene3_midian.html) landed on Scene 3's COVER — Jane: "there is only 1 cover image, before scene 1; between every scene there is only the journey tracker, no cover images." Scene 2 now navigates with ?from=scene2 and Scene 3 mirrors Scene 2's auto-launch: on ?from=scene2 OR an already-unlocked bundle it skips the cover + access gate straight into the opening cinematic (cover only shows on a cold standalone open). (c) Scene 3 tutorial/onboarding modal was a leftover BLUE gradient that clashed with Midian — converted to the warm gold/brown chrome matching .dialog-modal. (d) Scene 3 OPENING narration cinematic rebuilt to match Scene 1 — Jane: "i am not seeing the correct narration panel audio and image... the logic should be per the narration document. the style of showing the narration panels should be like how we do it for scene 1. for desktop there is a different size, for portrait and landscape there is different." The old opening was an off-script 4-panel "ACT III" text deck with NO image/audio swap and NO responsive panel sizing. Replaced CIN_PANELS with 